---
// COMPONENTS
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import SimplePage from "@/components/SimplePage.astro";

// DATA
import { baseData, mailtoHref } from "@/data/siteData";
---

<Layout
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy | Chris Nervegna"
  description="What christophernervegna.com collects, why, and who it's shared with. Short version: very little."
  hideChat
>
  <SimplePage
    bubble="The fine print"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lead="This is a personal portfolio site. It collects very little, and none of it is sold."
    updated="November 2026"
  >
    <div class="terms__content">
      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages you send.</strong> If you use the contact form, I get your name, email,
          the company and role you enter, and your message. Netlify handles the form.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Questions you ask the chat.</strong> The &ldquo;Ask about Chris&rdquo; box sends
          your question to Anthropic&rsquo;s API through a Netlify function to write the answer. I
          don&rsquo;t ask for your name there, so please don&rsquo;t include personal details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic analytics.</strong> When analytics are turned on, Google Analytics and
          Ahrefs record anonymous visit data like pages viewed, referring site, device type and
          rough location.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I use it</h2>
      <p>
        To reply to you, to see which parts of the site people find useful, and to keep the site
        running. That&rsquo;s it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it&rsquo;s shared with</h2>
      <p>
        Only the services that run the site: Netlify (hosting and forms), Anthropic (chat answers),
        and Google and Ahrefs (analytics). I don&rsquo;t sell or rent your information to anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can block analytics with your browser or an extension, and the site still works. To ask
        what I have from you or to have it deleted, email <a href={mailtoHref}>{baseData.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>
    </div>
  </SimplePage>
</Layout>
